# Build context exclusions.
#
# The context is sent to the daemon before the first instruction runs, so
# anything large and irrelevant here is latency on every build. Two entries
# matter more than the rest: `.venv` is hundreds of megabytes of the wrong
# platform's wheels, and `data/index` is a rebuilt artefact whose presence in
# the context would silently shadow the one the build produces.

# --- environments and caches ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# --- version control and tooling ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.claude/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# --- generated data ---
# The image builds these itself in the assets stage (or fetches them from S3 at
# runtime). Shipping a locally built index into the context risks baking a
# stale one that was never produced by this build.
data/index/
data/index-cache/
data/aiops.db
data/eval/latest_report.json

# LogHub samples are fetched by scripts/fetch_loghub.sh during the build. They
# are ~2.7MB of third-party logs and do not belong in the context.
data/logs/external/

# --- local configuration and secrets ---
# .env would otherwise be copied into a layer and shipped to a registry.
.env
.env.*
!env.example

# --- infrastructure and docs, not needed to run ---
infra/
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# --- editor/IDE ---
.vscode/
.idea/
